              "text": "You can download the latest version of Python directly from the official Python website:\n\n* **Official Downloads Page:** **[python.org/downloads](https://www.python.org/downloads/)**\n\n### Current Version Information\nThe latest stable version of Python is **Python 3.14.5**. \n\n### How to Install It on Your Operating System:\n\n* **Windows:** \n  1. Go to the official download page and click the **\"Download Python 3.14.5\"** button.\n  2. Run the downloaded `.exe` installer.\n  3. **Important:** Before clicking \"Install Now,\" make sure to check the box at the bottom that says **\"Add Python.exe to PATH.\"** This ensures you can run Python from your Command Prompt or PowerShell without configuration issues.\n\n* **macOS:**\n  1. Click the download button on the website to get the `.pkg` installer.\n  2. Run the installer and follow the on-screen prompts.\n\n* **Linux / Unix:**\n  Most Linux distributions come with Python pre-installed, though it might be an older version. To get the latest version, it is usually best to use your package manager (e.g., `apt` for Debian/Ubuntu, `dnf` for Fedora, or `pacman` for Arch) or build it from the official source code provided on the downloads page.",
